  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Feasibility Study and Pilot Project Integrated Real Time Water Monitoring System, through Government of China (P.R.C.)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USTDA is contributing $589,466 to partially fund a Feasibility Study (FS) for the Changjiang Water Resources Commission (CWRC) of China on an Integrated Real Time Water Monitoring System. The FS and pilot assess the technical and financial feasibility of installing a water monitoring system in the Han River Basin. Such a system would positively impact the environment of the entire Tangtze River Basin as well as help ensure clean drinking water for large populations in Northern China. CWRC and the Sutron Corporation (Sterling, VA), the sole source contractor, are sharing costs on the FS.</narrative>
  </description>
